        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1d800951-1ea4-5429-8293-ab64ca2704c7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: Project Sabre II\n- Products: Chengdu J-7, PAC JF-17 Thunder, CAC FC-1 Xiaolong, Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, MiG-21FL\n- Organizations: Pakistan Air Force, Pakistan Aeronautical Complex, Chengdu Aircraft Corporation\n- Concepts: successor aircraft, joint development, multirole combat jet\n\nFacts:\n- Project Sabre II was a Pakistan Air Force program to develop a feasible, low-cost multirole combat jet based on the Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, which was a Chinese variant of the MiG-21FL.\n- The PAC JF-17 Thunder, also called the CAC FC-1 Xiaolong, is a lightweight, single-engine, multirole combat aircraft developed jointly by the Pakistan Aeronautical Complex and the Chengdu Aircraft Corporation of China.\n- The Chengdu J-7 was extensively redeveloped into the CAC/PAC JF-17 Thunder, which became a successor to the Chengdu J-7 type.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "face8387-292b-55e7-b515-2c4b61010627",
        "text": "Page: Chengdu J-7. Sentence: The J-7 was extensively re-developed into the CAC/PAC JF-17 Thunder, which became a successor to the type.\nPage: CAC/PAC JF-17 Thunder. Sentence: The PAC JF-17 Thunder (Urdu: جے ایف-١٧ گرج‎ ), or CAC FC-1 \"Xiaolong\" (), is a lightweight, single-engine, multi-role combat aircraft developed jointly by the Pakistan Aeronautical Complex (PAC) and the Chengdu Aircraft Corporation (CAC) of China.\nPage: Project Sabre II. Sentence: Project Sabre II was the Pakistan Air Force's program to develop a feasible and low-cost multirole combat jet based on an existing design - the Chengdu F-7 Skybolt, a Chinese variant of the MiG–21FL.",
